<p class="copy">
	Among the largest ships operated by many navies, cruisers are often the flagship vessels of a fleet. Combining thick armor with overbuilt point-defense systems, cruisers serve as the centerpiece and command ship of a formation. While less heavily armed per ton than a <?php echo sf_lore_link('frigates', 'frigate'); ?>, they carry some of the heaviest individual weapons found aboard any ship.
</p>
<p class="copy">
	Cruisers are built to project national sovereignty as much as military power, carrying the production capabilities and Switch Gates required for near-limitless mission endurance. Their broad mission profile gives them luxurious cabins for diplomatic missions, medical facilities capable of supporting hospital operations, and docking space for numerous <?php echo sf_lore_link('trucks', 'trucks'); ?>, <?php echo sf_lore_link('cutters', 'cutters'); ?>, and <?php echo sf_lore_link('corvettes', 'corvettes'); ?>. For nations with interstellar territories, cruisers are sometimes equipped with LFGs, though the expense and internal volume required make this a compromise better left to the larger <?php echo sf_lore_link('starcruisers', 'Starcruiser'); ?> class.
</p>
